L2 Knowledge Base - Issue 3 (Copilot Access Concern)
v 1.0, 07/08/2026, status : Draft

Purpose
Handle unexpected Copilot matter exposure as a potential access-control concern until disproven.

Trigger
Use when a user reports seeing matter content they believe they should not access.

Required access
- Incident and security workflow access
- Source-system permission administration access
- Audit log access for source repository and related services

Procedure (navigation > action > expected)
1. Service desk > Incident > Open ticket > Set security severity flag.
Expected: concern is tracked as potential exposure.
2. Service desk > Work notes > Record user, time, matter ID/name, prompt text, surface.
Expected: minimum evidence baseline captured.
3. Ticket attachments > Store screenshot/context artifacts.
Expected: evidence preserved.
4. Source admin portal > Matter permissions > Check effective permissions for user.
Expected: intended vs actual access validated.
5. Source audit logs > Access/share/permission changes around event time.
Expected: unexpected grant/change evidence identified or excluded.
6. Copilot retrieval/audit path (if available) > Validate source alignment.
Expected: retrieval path correlation established.
7. If unauthorized access confirmed, revoke unintended access immediately.
Expected: containment applied.
8. If stale indexing/sync confirmed, correct permissions then reindex/republish.
Expected: surfaced content aligns to corrected permissions.
9. Run negative test (reporting user) and positive control test (authorized user).
Expected: unauthorized access blocked, authorized access preserved.

Verification
- Reporting user cannot retrieve unauthorized matter content.
- Authorized user behavior remains correct.
- Audit trail reflects corrective actions and no new unexpected exposure.

Rollback
1. Restore last known-good permission model from approved backup/change record if regression occurs.
2. Re-run reporting and control tests.
3. Escalate to security governance if impact expands.

Critical note
Do not close as harmless AI behavior without source permission and audit validation.
